<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🐟 LIVE LAKE TROUT DISTRIBUTION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LAKE TROUT — LIVE MODELED DISTRIBUTION</h2><p>Live modeled distribution estimate based on current environmental conditions, known species behavior, movement knowledge, and available telemetry evidence. This layer does not represent a census or confirmed presence of individual fish.</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/gamefish_lake_trout/legend.png?v=gfish-2026-09-26-glsea-Sat-26-Sep-2026-06-50-58-GMT-a96bbab58753-m1.1.0-r2" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Modeled distribution / habitat index: LOW <b>0</b> (transparent) &rarr; HIGH <b>1</b>. Current mean: <b>0.3508</b>, p95: <b>0.5108</b>, confidence/support: <b>0.795</b>. Telemetry events: <b>0</b> (+748 behavioral-prior receivers). Transparency marks low confidence or water outside the modeled domain.</p><p><b>Method:</b> telemetry evidence &times; seasonal migration &times; thermal suitability &times; diel behavior &times; habitat &times; movement corridors (weighted mean; confidence-gated transparency). Telemetry is behavioral evidence only &mdash; never abundance; it decays spatially and temporally, and unresolved tags stay unresolved.</p><p><b>Reading the gradient:</b> LOW (transparent) &rarr; HIGH (saturated) modeled distribution / habitat index. Transparency marks low confidence or water outside the modeled domain; a strong color with weak support fades toward transparent.</p><p><b>Sources:</b> NOAA/GLERL CoastWatch GLSEA lake surface temperature (<a href="https://apps.glerl.noaa.gov/coastwatch/webdata/glsea/cur/glsea_cur.asc">GLSEA current analysis</a>) and acoustic-telemetry evidence from <a href="https://github.com/wyattleathorn7/great-lakes-live-fish-telemetry">great-lakes-live-fish-telemetry</a> (USGS real-time receivers and GLATOS deployments; read as input, never modified).</p><p><b>Limitations:</b> surface temperature only (no depth resolution); shore-proximity habitat proxy with no bathymetry, substrate, or vegetation layers; telemetry decay constants are documented modeling assumptions.</p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers stay visible. Turn on/off independently of other layers.</p>]]></description>
    <GroundOverlay>
      <name>🐟 LIVE LAKE TROUT DISTRIBUTION</name>
      <drawOrder>10</drawOrder>
      <Icon>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/gamefish_lake_trout/current.png?v=gfish-2026-09-26-glsea-Sat-26-Sep-2026-06-50-58-GMT-a96bbab58753-m1.1.0-r2</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>21600</refreshInterval>
      </Icon>
      <LatLonBox>
        <north>49.5</north>
        <south>40.5</south>
        <east>-73.5</east>
        <west>-93.0</west>
      </LatLonBox>
    </GroundOverlay>
  </Document>
